1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,833
Parquet is a file format. Iceberg is not.
10 formats, 25 seconds.

2
00:00:01,833 --> 00:00:03,944
Row-based files
CSV: plain-text rows, comma-separated

3
00:00:03,944 --> 00:00:06,056
JSON: text format for structured data
JSON Lines: one JSON value per line

4
00:00:06,056 --> 00:00:08,167
Avro: binary rows, schema embedded

5
00:00:08,167 --> 00:00:10,900
Columnar + in-memory
Parquet: column-oriented file, built-in compression

6
00:00:10,900 --> 00:00:13,633
ORC: columnar file, created for Hive
Arrow: columnar in memory, built for compute

7
00:00:13,633 --> 00:00:16,816
Table formats: metadata over data files
Delta Lake: ACID transaction log

8
00:00:16,816 --> 00:00:20,000
Iceberg: snapshots, schema evolution, time travel
Hudi: upserts, deletes, incremental processing

9
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:22,733
File format: how bytes sit in a file
Table format: which files form the table

10
00:00:22,733 --> 00:00:25,467
Files store data. Tables track files.
